# Shenron City — environment
# Copy to .env. Nothing here is a secret, and nothing here should become one.

# ── Where Mission Control lives ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# The API the world reads its state from. Requests are proxied through the dev
# server so they stay same-origin, which is why this can point anywhere without
# touching the backend's CORS allowlist.
#
# MISSION_CONTROL_URL=http://127.0.0.1:9120

# Port the game itself serves on.
# GAME_PORT=9122

# ── Credentials ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# There are none, deliberately.
#
# The game never talks to a model provider. It talks to Mission Control, which
# already owns provider keys and reads them from its own agent home. A key
# placed in this file would be compiled into the browser bundle and readable by
# anyone who opens devtools.
#
# If you are about to add one here, the thing you want lives behind the backend.
